[
  {
    "pkheadingid": 475,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Definition",
    "headingPosition": 1,
    "headingid": 432,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67669,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 432,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Thymolipoma is an encapsulated tumour that consists of mature adipose tissue with interspersed non-neoplastic thymic tissue.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 476,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-O coding",
    "headingPosition": 2,
    "headingid": 433,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67670,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 433,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>8850/0 Thymolipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 477,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "ICD-11 coding",
    "headingPosition": 3,
    "headingid": 434,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67671,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 434,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>2E80.Y &amp; XH4G31 Other specified benign lipomatous neoplasm &amp; XH4G31 Thymolipoma</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 478,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Related terminology",
    "headingPosition": 4,
    "headingid": 435,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67672,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 435,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Not recommended:</em> thymolipomatous hamartoma.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 479,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Subtype(s)",
    "headingPosition": 5,
    "headingid": 436,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67673,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 436,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 480,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 437,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67674,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 437,
        "headingText": "<p>Thymolipomas occur mostly in the anterior (prevascular) mediastinum.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T13:01:33"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 481,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 438,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67675,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 438,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most thymolipomas are detected incidentally; others are found as a result of local symptoms (e.g. cough, dyspnoea, chest pain, hoarseness, and cyanosis) or paraneoplastic syndromes. Myasthenia gravis is the most common paraneoplastic syndrome {3051856; 8090879; 17444169}; aplastic anaemia, Graves disease, and hypogammaglobulinaemia are rare {17986126; 7116295}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 482,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 439,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67676,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 439,
        "headingText": "<p>Thymolipomas are rare tumours of the anterior (prevascular) mediastinum, accounting for 2&ndash;9% of all thymic neoplasms. The tumours can occur at any age, with no sex predominance {8539231; 20107952}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-04T13:01:52"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 483,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 440,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67677,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 440,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Theories postulated for the development of thymolipoma include a benign tumour of specialized thymic stroma (fat) arising in relation with the thymic epithelium, an aberrant development of the third pharyngeal pouch, and fatty regression of a hyperplastic thymus or thymoma {20107952; 9255058; 19433298}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 484,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 441,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67678,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 441,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>In one case, translocation involving the <em>HMGA2</em> gene on chromosome&nbsp;12q15 was found {19433298}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 491,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 448,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67679,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 448,
        "headingText": "<p>Thymolipomas are encapsulated tumours. They range in size from 30 to &gt;&nbsp;300 mm {20107952; 27293949; 26557924}. The tumours are fairly well circumscribed, soft, and yellow on cut surface. Scattered streaks or solid areas representing entrapped thymic tissue may be evident on gross inspection.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2021-02-01T10:26:37"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 485,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 442,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67680,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 442,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Histologically, the tumours consist of mature adipose tissue with strands or even large areas of thymic tissue that is mostly atrophic but may contain lymphoid follicles and Hassall corpuscles. Atypia and mitotic activity are absent. Thymolipomas may rarely contain thymomas or neuroendocrine tumours (NETs) {23992709; 22791779; 26517631}. Immunohistochemistry is usually not necessary.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 486,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 443,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67681,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 443,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Cytological smears or FNA specimens show few if any lymphocytes and scattered epithelial cells {23902624}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 487,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 444,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67682,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 444,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 490,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 447,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67683,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 447,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>An encapsulated tumour consisting of mature fat and thymic tissue, usually atrophic</li>\r\n</ul>",
        "timestamp": "2021-01-11T10:34:45"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 488,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 445,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67684,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 445,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 489,
    "bookid": 35,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 446,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 67685,
        "bookId": 35,
        "chapterId": 175,
        "headingId": 446,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Complete resection is curative. No metastases, recurrences, or tumour-related deaths have been reported.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-12-03T16:48:18"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]